{
  "_comment": [
    "The shrine-keeper at a shrine nothing has happened to yet.",
    "",
    "The ledger scene (shrine_keeper) is about a shortfall the players caused, which",
    "is the whole consequence-comedy engine of this mod: you are asked, very politely,",
    "to help with the paperwork for your own deicide. Diluting its opening line so it",
    "also worked at an untouched shrine would have cost the best thing about it. So",
    "there are two scenes and the keeper picks.",
    "",
    "This one is dramatic irony and nothing else. The keeper is CONTENT. The ledger",
    "balances, the quarter is closing, and they are pleased somebody came. Three feet",
    "away is a chest, and opening it kills God.",
    "",
    "The warning is real and is delivered as an apology for the housekeeping: the box",
    "opens for the one it is addressed to, nobody has come in a very long time, and",
    "the keeper keeps it tidy anyway because it would be embarrassing otherwise. A",
    "player will read that as flavour and open the chest. That is the design. The",
    "world told you, in a tone so mild you did not register it as being told.",
    "",
    "Dread covenant: not ominous, not winking, not foreshadowing at the audience. The",
    "keeper is sincere and slightly apologetic, and the scene is funny only in the way",
    "counter service at a dead institution is funny."
  ],
